==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|suppressus|lang=la}}, perfect passive participle of {{term|supprimo|supprimō|press down or under|lang=la}}, from {{term|sub||under|lang=la}} + {{term|premo|premō|press|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/səˈprɛs/}}
* {{audio|En-us-suppress.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɛs}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|suppresses|suppressing|suppressed}}

# To [[hold]] in place, to keep [[low]], to prevent publication.
#: ''The government '''suppressed''' the findings of their research about the true state of the economy.''
# {{US|legal}} To [[forbid]] the use of [[evidence]] at [[trial]] because it is [[improper]] or was improperly obtained.

====Related terms====
* [[suppression]]
* [[suppressor]]

